      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the area of figure \\(ABCD\\), we first need to understand the shape and area of each sector and then calculate the total area.\n\n1. **Identify the shape and the sectors:**\n   - Figure \\(ABCD\\) consists of two sectors of a circle with radius 12.\n   - Each sector has a central angle of \\(60^\\circ\\).\n   - The total angle in a circle is \\(360^\\circ\\), so two sectors cover \\(60^\\circ + 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ\\) of the circle.\n\n2. **Calculate the area of one sector:**\n   - The formula for the area of a sector of a circle is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of sector} = \\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi r^2\n     \\]\n     where \\(\\theta\\) is the central angle in degrees and \\(r\\) is the radius of the circle.\n   - Here, \\(\\theta = 60^\\circ\\) and \\(r = 12\\).\n   - Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of one sector} = \\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi \\times 12^2 = \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\pi \\times 144 = 24\\pi\n     \\]\n   - Since there are two such sectors, the total area of the two sectors is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total area} = 2 \\times 24\\pi = 48\\pi\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of figure \\(ABCD\\) is \\(\\boxed{48\\pi}\\).",
